What's going on?

2209
00:10:02,667 --> 00:10:04,667
So many problems...

2210
00:10:04,667 --> 00:10:06,797
I have to process a lot of things.

2211
00:10:07,087 --> 00:10:09,047
So many people have died.

2212
00:10:09,047 --> 00:10:10,797
Did they get an infection?

2213
00:10:10,797 --> 00:10:11,547
Or is it-

2214
00:10:11,007 --> 00:10:14,177
It was a chore just getting the
 immigrant sector quarantined too...

2215
00:10:15,097 --> 00:10:20,307
and now I have this much data related
 to that ADW Project that I have to check.

2216
00:10:20,307 --> 00:10:22,687
It's enough to complain about.

2217
00:10:23,397 --> 00:10:26,687
Well, I just have to authorize them.

2218
00:10:28,987 --> 00:10:31,027
ADW Project?

2219
00:10:31,027 --> 00:10:34,077
This is our first time under martial law too.

2220
00:10:34,077 --> 00:10:36,997
Even if the Security Bureau now has control...

2221
00:10:37,787 --> 00:10:40,917
Oh, by the way, the Bureau Chief you spoke about...

2222
00:10:40,917 --> 00:10:44,417
He's a wisecracker, that's for sure. Real sharp.

2223
00:10:53,047 --> 00:10:56,267
Where is he... Where is Raul Creed?

2224
00:10:56,267 --> 00:10:57,557
No idea...

2225
00:10:58,137 --> 00:11:01,147
But being too sharp is a problem.

2226
00:11:01,147 --> 00:11:03,397
Think about the ones who have to deal with him...

2227
00:11:03,397 --> 00:11:06,027
I have so much more busywork.

2228
00:11:03,397 --> 00:11:04,767
What is my grandfather...

2229
00:11:06,437 --> 00:11:08,527
What is the Administrator doing?

2230
00:11:08,817 --> 00:11:10,107
Oh, I know.

2231
00:11:10,107 --> 00:11:12,027
I should ask you to pass this on.

2232
00:11:12,567 --> 00:11:14,277
Please take this.

2233
00:11:14,577 --> 00:11:20,207
This data from the Health Bureau
 pertains to the side effects of ADW.

2234
00:11:20,787 --> 00:11:22,827
Please deliver this to the Administrator.

2235
00:11:23,627 --> 00:11:25,837
I dare not tell him this myself...

2236
00:11:25,837 --> 00:11:27,167
What do you mean?

2237
00:11:27,167 --> 00:11:28,877
It was a total failure.

2238
00:11:29,377 --> 00:11:31,717
The mortality rate was 90 percent, you see.

2239
00:11:31,717 --> 00:11:34,297
The name of the genius Daedalus Yumeno is now mud.

2240
00:11:35,757 --> 00:11:39,977
What need was there for us to change anyway?

2241
00:11:40,477 --> 00:11:44,147
Model citizens need only protect the order of the Dome.

2242
00:11:44,437 --> 00:11:46,267
It's business as usual.

2243
00:11:47,017 --> 00:11:50,897
We just need to do business as usual... the way we usually do.

2244
00:11:51,737 --> 00:11:53,357
Don't forget them tomorrow, okay?

2245
00:11:54,987 --> 00:11:56,907
Your primary care physician's papers.

2246
00:12:00,907 --> 00:12:02,327
Take care.

2247
00:12:05,287 --> 00:12:10,757
<i>Dependent on Entourages, the
 collective, and the Administrator for everything,</i>

2248
00:12:11,377 --> 00:12:15,887
<i>and ignoring the truth - so this is the model citizens' fate.</i>

2249
00:12:17,847 --> 00:12:18,887
Re-l!

2250
00:12:18,887 --> 00:12:20,307
I've been looking for you.

2251
00:12:21,177 --> 00:12:22,347
Daedalus.

2252
00:12:22,977 --> 00:12:25,017
So this is where you were.

2253
00:12:25,017 --> 00:12:26,727
Always roaming around...

2254
00:12:26,727 --> 00:12:28,147
Now, come with me.

2255
00:12:30,227 --> 00:12:31,437
Daedalus?

2256
00:13:23,997 --> 00:13:25,747
Monad PROXY...

2257
00:13:43,217 --> 00:13:45,137
I'm the one who killed you.

2258
00:13:45,677 --> 00:13:48,307
But how could you have taken this so far?

2259
00:13:49,057 --> 00:13:50,647
Donov Mayer!

2260
00:14:11,957 --> 00:14:13,337
The answer is PROXY One.

2261
00:14:17,337 --> 00:14:19,047
PROXY One!

2262
00:14:20,927 --> 00:14:22,257
Are you sad?

2263
00:14:32,817 --> 00:14:33,857
These...

2264
00:14:37,947 --> 00:14:39,607
They're pretty.

2265
00:14:40,857 --> 00:14:44,987
Why do you not fear me in this form?

2266
00:14:45,577 --> 00:14:46,617
Why?

2267
00:14:47,157 --> 00:14:48,497
Why should I?

2268
00:14:48,497 --> 00:14:51,247
You have such a gentle face.

2269
00:14:51,957 --> 00:14:54,037
What do I need to fear?

2270
00:14:54,377 --> 00:14:55,837
They're a matched pair.

2271
00:14:55,837 --> 00:14:57,837
Are they both yours?

2272
00:14:57,837 --> 00:15:01,177
One... seems to be Monad's.

2273
00:15:01,637 --> 00:15:04,557
You loved Monad, didn't you.

2274
00:15:07,717 --> 00:15:09,057
I pity you.

2275
00:15:10,437 --> 00:15:13,857
Because I love Monad too.

2276
00:15:15,017 --> 00:15:16,567
Who are you?

2277
00:15:17,567 --> 00:15:20,067
I am Re-l Mayer.

2278
00:15:20,067 --> 00:15:21,907
What are you saying?

2279
00:15:22,947 --> 00:15:25,737
Oh, but I...

2280
00:15:32,327 --> 00:15:33,577
am Re-l Mayer!

2281
00:15:52,557 --> 00:15:54,187
I wonder what's wrong with me.

2282
00:15:54,187 --> 00:15:56,767
Oh, so that was Vincent!

2283
00:15:58,727 --> 00:16:00,067
That must be it!

2284
00:16:06,777 --> 00:16:08,197
Daedalus...

2285
00:16:08,197 --> 00:16:09,117
I'm sorry.

2286
00:16:09,787 --> 00:16:15,917
Re-l, you don't need to imitate that bad girl so much.

2287
00:16:15,917 --> 00:16:17,667
You are yourself.

2288
00:16:19,507 --> 00:16:24,127
In the end, I couldn't fulfill any of my promises.

2289
00:16:25,087 --> 00:16:29,307
I could neither capture the PROXY
 we were after, nor collect the subject...

2290
00:16:29,637 --> 00:16:32,477
Re-l, are you still rambling on about that?

2291
00:16:32,477 --> 00:16:36,187
Acting as though you've overwritten
 yourself with the previous model's data...

2292
00:16:36,187 --> 00:16:37,397
What are you talking about?

2293
00:16:37,397 --> 00:16:41,897
Did you steal data from a terminal to surprise me?

2294
00:16:41,897 --> 00:16:43,147
Goodness.

2295
00:16:43,607 --> 00:16:46,027
I dislike it when you do things like that.

2296
00:16:46,027 --> 00:16:47,527
Please tell me!

2297
00:16:47,527 --> 00:16:49,947
What's behind the rapid decrease
 in population over such a short time?

2298
00:16:49,947 --> 00:16:52,117
What is the ADW Project?

2299
00:16:52,617 --> 00:16:54,287
I heard it from the Bureau Chief!

2300
00:16:54,287 --> 00:16:55,667
What did you do to the citizens?!

2301
00:16:57,127 --> 00:16:58,377
You're hurting me.

2302
00:16:59,667 --> 00:17:01,087
I'm sorry.

2303
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:02,707
Who are you?

2304
00:17:02,707 --> 00:17:04,217
What do you mean?

2305
00:17:04,217 --> 00:17:05,797
You're not my Re-l.

2306
00:17:06,337 --> 00:17:07,337
Daedalus...

2307
00:17:07,337 --> 00:17:08,427
I get it...

2308
00:17:08,757 --> 00:17:10,137
You're...

2309
00:17:11,097 --> 00:17:12,517
the traitor.

2310
00:17:14,137 --> 00:17:15,347
Re-l!

2311
00:17:15,977 --> 00:17:17,347
Come out here!

2312
00:17:17,347 --> 00:17:18,267
Daedalus!

2313
00:17:18,807 --> 00:17:20,267
You're hurting me. Let go!

2314
00:17:22,147 --> 00:17:23,397
Answer me!

2315
00:17:29,827 --> 00:17:31,157
How's it looking?

2316
00:17:31,157 --> 00:17:32,447
A lot of 'em.

2317
00:17:35,617 --> 00:17:38,287
Chief, that one looks familiar.

2318
00:17:38,287 --> 00:17:39,627
Let's see...

2319
00:17:42,457 --> 00:17:44,417
Oh my!

2320
00:17:44,417 --> 00:17:46,967
Looks like a chance for a special promotion!

2321
00:17:47,877 --> 00:17:51,257
With this, I'll finally redeem myself...

2322
00:18:12,527 --> 00:18:15,247
You didn't come here until now.

2323
00:18:15,747 --> 00:18:18,617
And now, it's too late.

2324
00:18:18,617 --> 00:18:21,247
What do you intend to do now?

2325
00:18:21,247 --> 00:18:23,627
The time has already ended,

2326
00:18:25,917 --> 00:18:27,717
Creator.

2327
00:18:41,857 --> 00:18:44,227
The Womb System has fallen silent.

2328
00:18:44,817 --> 00:18:46,527
You know why, don't you?

2329
00:18:46,937 --> 00:18:51,027
The absence of Monad... no, Vincent.

2330
00:18:51,317 --> 00:18:57,197
So Raul started saying that we don't need PROXIES if we change.

2331
00:18:57,787 --> 00:18:59,497
That's the ADW Project.

2332
00:18:59,917 --> 00:19:02,247
Put simply, it's body modification.

2333
00:19:02,787 --> 00:19:04,417
As if such a thing is possible.

2334
00:19:04,417 --> 00:19:08,167
Then, knowing it would fail, you-

2335
00:19:07,257 --> 00:19:08,167
By the way,

2336
00:19:08,167 --> 00:19:11,427
the pillar of light you spoke of... That's Rapture.

2337
00:19:11,967 --> 00:19:17,267
You see, Raul couldn't live with the fact that we were the losers.

2338
00:19:17,927 --> 00:19:19,137
Losers?

2339
00:19:20,097 --> 00:19:21,477
The winners, huh.

2340
00:19:22,557 --> 00:19:27,317
Since you're here, it must mean <i>he</i> is still alive.

2341
00:19:29,187 --> 00:19:31,447
Let me tell you something helpful.

2342
00:19:31,447 --> 00:19:35,027
The one who ordered the attack on you here wasn't Raul,

2343
00:19:35,577 --> 00:19:37,077
surprisingly enough.

2344
00:19:37,077 --> 00:19:38,617
What do you mean?

2345
00:19:40,707 --> 00:19:42,577
This is as far as I go.

2346
00:19:42,577 --> 00:19:45,337
Try asking the man himself.

2347
00:19:45,837 --> 00:19:47,167
Grandfather...?

2348
00:19:50,797 --> 00:19:53,547
Grandfather gave the order.

2349
00:19:57,307 --> 00:20:00,597
You are Raul's Entourage!

2350
00:20:06,687 --> 00:20:09,107
The Administrator loved.

2351
00:20:09,397 --> 00:20:12,147
The Creator founded Romdeau...

2352
00:20:12,147 --> 00:20:13,777
And created us.

2353
00:20:13,777 --> 00:20:15,567
He gave us autoreivs...

2354
00:20:15,567 --> 00:20:18,027
And gave us the ability to have children.

2355
00:20:18,027 --> 00:20:20,287
The Administrator hated.

2356
00:20:20,747 --> 00:20:23,707
Why do we exist?

2357
00:20:23,707 --> 00:20:26,917
Who will ease our solitude?

2358
00:20:26,917 --> 00:20:29,337
Why did you abandon us?

2359
00:20:29,337 --> 00:20:32,127
Why did you not love us?

2360
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:36,547
The Administrator sought.

2361
00:20:36,547 --> 00:20:38,637
Not the Creator...

2362
00:20:38,927 --> 00:20:40,637
But the entity we seized...

2363
00:20:40,637 --> 00:20:42,637
Monad PROXY.

2364
00:20:42,977 --> 00:20:47,147
The Creator returned to us, unbeknownst...

2365
00:20:47,437 --> 00:20:49,647
As an immigrant from Mosk.

2366
00:20:49,647 --> 00:20:52,397
The Creator took Monad from us...

2367
00:20:52,397 --> 00:20:54,277
And departed once again.

2368
00:20:54,277 --> 00:20:57,697
The Creator thinks, therefore we are.

2369
00:20:57,697 --> 00:21:02,787
No matter how <i>we</i> thought, the Creator was already gone.

2370
00:21:02,787 --> 00:21:05,997
And now, he returns to be with us for the third time.

2371
00:21:09,587 --> 00:21:11,167
We desire...

2372
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:14,417
The world does not exist where the Creator does not think of it.

2373
00:21:14,417 --> 00:21:16,797
We desire that you think of us.

2374
00:21:16,797 --> 00:21:19,547
We think, therefore we are.

